/T (21.1. Income earned by content creators, social media influencers, and other similar digital income earners, whether from within or outside Nigeria, from their trade, business, profession, or vocation, is chargeable to tax. 21.2. The income shall be computed as gains or profits from a trade or business and shall include earnings from subscriptions, advertisements, brand endorsements, platform revenue sharing, digital rewards, and all forms of compensation, whether in money or money's worth. 21.3. Persons making payments to content creators, influencers, or their agents shall comply with all applicable withholding tax, reporting and remittance obligations.)
